Table full name: TCGA_HG38_DATA_V0.TCGA_BIOCLIN_V0.CLINICAL
Column name: tumor_type Type: TEXT Description: Tumor Type; e.g. Primary, Type 1, Type 2
Column name: vital_status Type: TEXT Description: Survival state of the participant; e.g. dead, alive
Column name: other_malignancy_type Type: TEXT Description: Indicates whether another malignancy occurred before or at the same time; e.g. Prior Malignancy, Synchronous Malignancy
Column name: person_neoplasm_cancer_status Type: TEXT Description: The participant's cancer status; e.g. With Tumor, Tumor Free
Column name: pathologic_N Type: TEXT Description: The pathologic N score is a rating of the extent of cancer within nearby lymph nodes, based on surgery or biopsy; e.g. N1, N2, N3
Column name: clinical_T Type: TEXT Description: The clinical T score is a rating of the extent of the primary tumor, based on results of tests done before surgery, such as physical exams and imaging scans; e.g. T1, T2, T3, T4
Column name: tss_code Type: TEXT Description: Tissue Source Site Code; see https://gdc.cancer.gov/resources-TCGA-users/TCGA-code-tables/tissue-source-site-codes for explanation of codes
Column name: pathologic_stage Type: TEXT Description: The stage of the cancer, based on surgery or biopsy; e.g. Stage I, Stage II, Stage III, Stage IV
Column name: psa_value Type: FLOAT Description: A male participant's Prostrate-Specific Antigen (PSA) value
Column name: other_malignancy_anatomic_site Type: TEXT Description: The site on the body where the other malignancy occurred; e.g. Bladder, Uterus, etc.
Column name: history_of_neoadjuvant_treatment Type: TEXT Description: Describes the patient's history of neoadjuvant treatment and the kind of treament given prior to resection of the tumor; e.g. Yes, Pharmaceutical Treatment Prior to Resection, etc.
Column name: age_at_diagnosis Type: NUMBER Description: Age, in years, at which a condition or disease was first diagnosed
Column name: icd_10 Type: TEXT Description: Alphanumeric value used to describe the disease code from the tenth version of the International Classification of Disease (ICD-10)
Column name: ethnicity Type: TEXT Description: The ethnic origination of a participant, independent from race; e.g. Not Hispanic or Latino, Hispanic or Latino
Column name: days_to_birth Type: NUMBER Description: Days since birth (a negative value, relative to the date of diagnosis which is considered to be t=0)
Column name: hpv_calls Type: TEXT Description: HPV strains; e.g. HPV18, HPV45, etc.
Column name: number_pack_years_smoked Type: FLOAT Description: The number of packs smoked per day times the number of years smoked by the participant
Column name: residual_tumor Type: TEXT Description: Status of the tissue margin following surgical resection; e.g. R0, R1, R2, RX
Column name: batch_number Type: NUMBER Description: The BCR Batch Code; see https://gdc.cancer.gov/resources-TCGA-users/TCGA-code-tables/bcr-batch-codes for explanation of the codes
Column name: program_name Type: TEXT Description: Program Name, always TCGA (The Cancer Genome Atlas) in this table.
Column name: case_barcode Type: TEXT Description: TCGA patient/case barcode; e.g. TCGA-06-0119
Column name: gleason_score_combined Type: NUMBER Description: The Gleason Score (ranging from 1 -5) is the grade of the aggressiveness of prostate cancer. The combined Gleason Score is the primary Gleason score  (for the largest area of the tumor) added to the secondary Gleason Score (for the next largest section of the tumor).
Column name: menopause_status Type: TEXT Description: A female participant's menopausal status; e.g. Post, Pre, Indeterminate, Peri
Column name: pregnancies Type: TEXT Description: The number of times (including currently if it applies) that a female participant has been pregnant, regardless of outcome.
Column name: clinical_N Type: TEXT Description: The clinical N score is a rating of the extent of cancer within nearby lymph nodes, based on results of tests done before surgery, such as physical exams and imaging scans; e.g. N1, N2, N3
Column name: clinical_M Type: TEXT Description: The clinical M score is a rating of metastasis, that is, how much cancer has spread to distant sites. It is based on results of tests done before surgery, such as physical exams and imaging scans; e.g. MX, M0, M1
Column name: primary_therapy_outcome_success Type: TEXT Description: Kind of outcome achieved after the completion of the initial course of treatment; e.g. Complete Remission/Response, Progressive Disease, etc.
Column name: other_dx Type: TEXT Description: Indicator and type of other diagnosis; e.g. No; Yes, History of Prior Malignancy; Yes, History of Synchronous/Bilateral Malignancy; Both History of Synchronous/Bilateral and Prior Malignancy
Column name: country Type: TEXT Description: Country of the participant; e.g. Germany, United States, Canada, etc.
Column name: days_to_submitted_specimen_dx Type: NUMBER Description: Numeric value to represent the day of the diagnosis for the submitted sample.
Column name: histological_type Type: TEXT Description: The histological type of cancer; e.g. Adenosquamous, Astrocytoma, etc.
Column name: race Type: TEXT Description: The race of a participant, independent from ethnicity; e.g. White, Black or African American, Asian, Native Hawaiian or other Pacific Islander, American Indian or Alaska Native
Column name: h_pylori_infection Type: TEXT Description: Indicator of previous or current diagnosis of Helicobactor pylori infection; e.g. Yes, No, Never, Current
Column name: new_tumor_event_after_initial_treatment Type: TEXT Description: Indicates whether a patient has had a new tumor event after initial treatment; Yes, No
Column name: days_to_last_known_alive Type: NUMBER Description: Number of days from the date of diagnosis to the last day on which a person was known to be alive. This field is a combination of the days_to_last_followup and days_to death fields. Therefore, this field can be used whether the vital_status is 'alive' or 'dead'.
Column name: program_dbgap_accession_number Type: TEXT Description: Program dbGaP accession number, eg phs000178
Column name: year_of_initial_pathologic_diagnosis Type: NUMBER Description: Four digit year of the initial pathologic diagnosis
Column name: icd_o_3_histology Type: TEXT Description: Code that represents the histology of the disease using the third edition of the International Classification of Diseases for Oncology, published in 2000, used principally in tumor and cancer registries for coding the site (topography) and the histology (morphology) of neoplasms
Column name: gender Type: TEXT Description: Participant gender; e.g. Male, Female
Column name: tumor_tissue_site Type: TEXT Description: The location on the body where the tumor exists; e.g. Brain, Ovary, Lung, etc.
Column name: tobacco_smoking_history Type: NUMBER Description: Category describing current smoking status and smoking history as self-reported by a participant.; e.g. 1, 2, etc.
Column name: number_of_lymphnodes_examined Type: NUMBER Description: The number of lymph nodes examined
Column name: age_began_smoking_in_years Type: NUMBER Description: Age, in years, that the participant began smoking
Column name: bcr Type: TEXT Description: Biospecimen Core Resource; e.g. Nationwide Children's Hospital, Washington University
Column name: history_of_colon_polyps Type: TEXT Description: Indicator if the participant had a previous history of colon polyps as noted in the history/physical or previous endoscopic report(s); e.g. Yes, No
Column name: stopped_smoking_year Type: NUMBER Description: Four-digit year that the participant stopped smoking; e.g. 2010
Column name: other_malignancy_histological_type Type: TEXT Description: The histological type of cancer of the other malignancy; e.g. Adenosquamous, Astrocytoma, etc.
Column name: lymphatic_invasion Type: TEXT Description: Indicator if small or thin-walled vessel invasion is present, indicating lymphatic involvement; e.g. Yes, No
Column name: year_of_tobacco_smoking_onset Type: NUMBER Description: Four-digit year that the participant started smoking; e.g. 2010
Column name: bmi Type: FLOAT Description: Body Mass Index of participant
Column name: disease_code Type: TEXT Description: A code representing the type of cancer. Values can be found at https://gdc.cancer.gov/resources-TCGA-users/TCGA-code-tables/TCGA-study-abbreviations; e.g. OV, GBM, LUAD
Column name: anatomic_neoplasm_subdivision Type: TEXT Description: The spatial location, subdivisions and/or atomic site name of a tumor; e.g. Rectum, Larynx, Tonsil, etc.
Column name: mononucleotide_and_dinucleotide_marker_panel_analysis_status Type: TEXT Description: Status of the mononucleotide and dinucleotide marker panel analysis; microsatellite-stable (MSS), low level MSI (MSI-L) if less than 40% of markers were altered and high level MSI (MSI-H) if greater than 40% of markers were altered
Column name: project_name Type: TEXT Description: Project Name; frequently the same as or similar to the project disease type eg   Acute Lymphoblastic Leukemia - Phase II   or   Breast Invasive Carcinoma   etc
Column name: days_to_last_followup Type: NUMBER Description: If vital_status indicates 'alive', then this is the number of days from the date of diagnosis to the last followup (communication contact).
Column name: neoplasm_histologic_grade Type: TEXT Description: Rating which expresses the degree of abnormality of cancer cells, a measure of differentiation and aggressiveness; e.g. G1, G2, G3, G4
Column name: days_to_death Type: NUMBER Description: If vital_status indicates 'dead', then this is the number of days to death (a positive value) relative to the date of diagnosis.
Column name: case_gdc_id Type: TEXT Description: GDC unique identifer for this case; e.g. 7b4ce492-ff40-4bf1-b3e8-75ff83e8746d. This identifier can be used to find more information at the GDC Data Portal ( https://portal.gdc.cancer.gov/cases/7b4ce492-ff40-4bf1-b3e8-75ff83e8746d )
Column name: primary_neoplasm_melanoma_dx Type: TEXT Description: Indicates whether a person had a primary diagnosis of melanoma; e.g. Yes, No
Column name: number_of_lymphnodes_positive_by_he Type: NUMBER Description: The number of lymph nodes involved with disease as determined by histological examination
Column name: height Type: FLOAT Description: Height of participant in centimeters
Column name: venous_invasion Type: TEXT Description: Indicator if large vessel or venous invasion was detected by surgery or presence in a tumor specimen; e.g. Yes, No
Column name: project_short_name Type: TEXT Description: Project name abbreviation; the program name appended with a project name abbreviation; e.g. TCGA-OV, etc.
Column name: days_to_initial_pathologic_diagnosis Type: NUMBER Description: The number of days to initial pathologic diagnosis
Column name: icd_o_3_site Type: TEXT Description: Code that represents the site of the disease using the third edition of the International Classification of Diseases for Oncology, published in 2000, used principally in tumor and cancer registries for coding the site (topography) and the histology (morphology) of neoplasms
Column name: pathologic_T Type: TEXT Description: The pathologic T score is a rating of the extent of the primary tumor, based on surgery or biopsy; e.g. T1, T2, T3, T4
Column name: colorectal_cancer Type: TEXT Description: Indicates whether the participant has colorectal cancer; e.g. Yes, No
Column name: weight Type: FLOAT Description: Weight of participant in kilograms
Column name: hpv_status Type: TEXT Description: Indicates whether the participant has a record of a positive finding for human papillomavirus; e.g. Positive, Negative, Indeterminate
Column name: pathologic_M Type: TEXT Description: The pathologic M score is a rating of metastasis, that is, how much cancer has spread to distant sites. It is based on surgery or biopsy; e.g. MX, M0, M1
Column name: lymphnodes_examined Type: TEXT Description: Indicator whether the lymph nodes were examined; e.g. Yes, No
Column name: lymphovascular_invasion_present Type: TEXT Description: Indicator if  invasion of a cancer to the blood vessels and/or lymphatics invasion is present; e.g. Yes, No
Column name: clinical_stage Type: TEXT Description: The stage of the cancer, based on results of tests done before surgery, such as physical exams and imaging scans; e.g. Stage I, Stage II, Stage III, Stage IV
